## 9. Timeline / Phasing

No hard external deadline — this is internal infrastructure, so phasing is effort-based, not date-driven.

```
Phase 0  Freeze this PRD + write ADRs for the open questions above       (before any P0 work starts)
Phase 1  Ship all P0 items                                                (target: one focused sprint)
Phase 2  Ship P1 items                                                    (target: following 2–4 weeks)
Phase 3  Revisit P2 only after Phase 1+2 are proven on 2+ real machines
         (at minimum: 1 native Linux host, 1 WSL host)
```

**Phase 1 is the hard gate.** Nothing in P1/P2 should start until every P0 acceptance criterion above is checked off — that ordering is the single most important recommendation carried forward from the architecture review chain.
